---
/** Privacy and control: what stays on your computer, what leaves only with your yes, and the two yeses. */
const stays = [
  ['Your folders and files', 'The agent sees one folder, in its own container.'],
  ['Conversations', 'Every session, its tool calls and their output.'],
  ['Keys', "In Clank's secrets, readable by you alone; never shown or logged."],
  ['Records', 'Every event, request and answer Clank kept.'],
  ['MCP servers marked local', 'Never offered to a cloud model.'],
  ['Notion pages', 'Never sent to a cloud model.'],
];
---

<section class="section" id="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy and control</p>
      <h2 id="privacy-title">Local by default.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        With a model on your GPU, nothing leaves your computer. With a cloud model, a workspace's requests leave only after
        two yeses, and you can see every one.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cols">
      <div class="col stays">
        <h3><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Stays on your computer</h3>
        <dl>
          {
            stays.map(([term, text]) => (
              <div>
                <dt>{term}</dt>
                <dd>{text}</dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
        <p class="also">
          The workspace's container reaches only Clank, never the internet unless you grant it. With a local model,
          nothing leaves at all.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="col leaves">
        <h3><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Leaves only with your yes</h3>
        <p>
          With a cloud model, the gateway sends a workspace's requests to OpenRouter, then to the model's provider. By
          default Clank asks only for providers that keep no data.
        </p>
        <p class="what">
          <b>What goes:</b> your messages, what the agent reads of the folder, command output, and its instructions.
        </p>

        <ol class="yeses">
          <li>
            <span class="n">1</span>
            <p><b>Once for OpenRouter.</b> What goes, where, and what never goes, read and agreed when you add the model.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="n">2</span>
            <p><b>Once for each workspace</b>, before its agent first uses the cloud:</p>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="ask" role="img" aria-label="Clank asks: Let my-project's agent use the cloud model? Press y to allow, or n to keep it local.">
          <p class="ask-q">Let my-project's agent use the cloud model?</p>
          <p class="ask-d">Its requests go to OpenRouter; Notion pages and local-only servers never do.</p>
          <p class="ask-k"><span><kbd class="key">y</kbd> allow</span><span><kbd class="key">n</kbd> keep local</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cols {
    margin-top: clamp(36px, 4.5vw, 56px);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 18px;
    padding: clamp(22px, 2.6vw, 32px);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .col h3 {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }

  .dot {
    width: 9px;
    height: 9px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--c);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px color-mix(in srgb, var(--c) 18%, transparent);
  }

  .stays {
    --c: var(--green);
  }

  .leaves {
    --c: var(--orange);
  }

  dl {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  dl div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.3fr);
    gap: 4px 18px;
    padding: 11px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  dt {
    color: var(--text-strong);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .also {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .leaves > p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .leaves b {
    color: var(--text-strong);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .what {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .yeses {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .yeses li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 28px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .yeses p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .n {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 26px;
    height: 26px;
    border-radius: 7px;
    border: 1px solid var(--orange);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--orange);
  }

  .ask {
    margin-left: 40px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--yellow);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--well);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.84rem;
  }

  .ask-q {
    color: var(--text-strong);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .ask-d {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .ask-k {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px 18px;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    dl div {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .ask {
      margin-left: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
